xnu 0403: the UI hook reaches kbd and Spotlight, the keyboard's processes

The software keyboard draws correctly-sized keys (42 pt on a 48 pt pitch, the
480 pt layout) but on its first presentation puts the ten-key row at x 37.3 pt
instead of 3, so `p`, delete and `search` are clipped by the right edge. The
cause is UIKit's phone keyboard width, not the host: measured 2026-11-21 in the
Spotlight process, the chain is UIInputSetHostView 480 -> _UIKBCompatInputView
480 -> UIKeyboardAutomatic 414 at x 33 -> UIKeyboardImpl 480 ->
UIKeyboardLayoutStar 480, and 414 pt is the widest iPhone keyboard centred in
the 480 pt window.

Which process lays that plane out was the open question. SpringBoard registers
the whole keyboard family (UIKeyboardLayoutStar, UIKeyboardLayout,
TUIKeyplaneView, UIKBKeyplaneView) and instantiates none of them for the
presented keyboard; kbd carries the input managers (TIKeyboard*) and no layout
class at all, even after the keyboard is up; the keyboard is laid out in the
Spotlight process (`MONDRIAN SURF: Spotlight ... 1440x729`), which hosts the
search UI and its keyboard. Bit 11 therefore gives the hook to both kbd and
Spotlight, and it is part of the default mask: mondrian_ui_hook=3334
(6 | 0x100 | 0x400 | 0x800). The hook, not the kernel, corrects the automatic's
frame (docs/UI_PERFORMANCE.md).

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
index 3dc87f4..6bfe386 100755
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5679,6 +5679,17 @@ bad:
  */
 #define MONDRIAN_HOOK_APP               0x400
 
+/*
+ * kbd and Spotlight (0x800): the two processes involved in the software
+ * keyboard. The keyboard is laid out in Spotlight; UIKit gives its
+ * UIKeyboardAutomatic a 414 pt phone keyboard and centres it on this 480 pt
+ * panel, which shifts the 480 pt impl to x 33 and clips the last column.
+ * SpringBoard registers the keyboard family and instantiates none of it, and
+ * kbd has no layout class, so both names carry the bit; the hook corrects the
+ * automatic's frame through UIView's setters (docs/UI_PERFORMANCE.md).
+ */
+#define MONDRIAN_HOOK_KBD               0x800
+
 /*
  * Does this boot's copy of a dylib exist in /private/var/vm? glblob=1 writes
  * them there once the root turns writable, so before that, or with glblob=0,
@@ -6110,6 +6121,12 @@ mondrian_ui_hook_env(struct image_params *imgp, char *env, size_t size)
